WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:03.930
Helpful pages, honest SEO, and measuring what works.

2
00:00:04.280 --> 00:00:07.780
This is the video for module three of the SEO course.

3
00:00:09.030 --> 00:00:15.800
Google says its systems aim to reward content made mainly to help people, not content made mainly to rank.

4
00:00:16.150 --> 00:00:25.340
People-first pages come from real experience, answer the customer's real question, and show clear prices, photos and local details.

5
00:00:26.590 --> 00:00:30.980
Search-first pages chase keywords, copy others and pad the word count.

6
00:00:31.330 --> 00:00:38.200
Many small-business pages fail simply because they say almost nothing: a heading, a photo, and call us.

7
00:00:39.450 --> 00:00:47.900
Google's rater guidelines talk about E-E-A-T: experience, expertise, authoritativeness and trust. Trust matters most.

8
00:00:48.250 --> 00:00:54.120
For a small business, that means simple, real things. Show who runs the business and where it is.

9
00:00:55.370 --> 00:01:06.100
Use real photos of your own work. A caterer who has cooked jollof for 300-guest weddings, with her own photos, shows experience a copied article cannot.

10
00:01:07.350 --> 00:01:16.860
Give your contact details and honest prices, and show genuine reviews. If you use AI to help write, check every fact and add your own experience.

11
00:01:18.110 --> 00:01:24.190
Google mainly looks at the mobile version of your page, and most visitors use phones on costly data.

12
00:01:24.540 --> 00:01:36.790
For example, Ifeoma sells Ankara dresses. In PageSpeed Insights, her collection page takes 6.8 seconds to show its main content. That measure is called LCP.

13
00:01:38.040 --> 00:01:51.560
Her 24 photos come straight from her phone, about 3 to 4 MB each. She resizes each to 1200 pixels wide and saves them as WebP, about 150 KB each.

14
00:01:52.810 --> 00:01:57.850
She turns on lazy loading, so lower photos only load when the visitor scrolls.

15
00:01:59.100 --> 00:02:03.340
She removes an auto-playing video and a chat plugin she never used.

16
00:02:04.590 --> 00:02:15.390
She retests. LCP is now 2.3 seconds, inside the Good range of 2.5 seconds or less, and the page costs visitors far less data.

17
00:02:16.640 --> 00:02:24.300
Some sellers promise fast results through tricks. Sites that break Google's spam policies may rank lower or disappear.

18
00:02:24.650 --> 00:02:34.570
Link spam means buying links that pass ranking credit. For example, Grace was offered 500 backlinks for 40,000 naira. She said no.

19
00:02:35.820 --> 00:02:40.170
Keyword stuffing means repeating words or lists of towns unnaturally.

20
00:02:41.420 --> 00:02:54.110
Hidden text and doorway pages try to fool Google. Instead, Grace listed her firm on her professional body's directory and wrote a useful article. She earned two genuine links, with no risk.

21
00:02:55.360 --> 00:03:06.460
The Performance report in Search Console shows clicks, impressions, average position and CTR. CTR means click-through rate: clicks divided by impressions.

22
00:03:07.710 --> 00:03:19.010
For example, Funke compares 3 months before and after fixing her birthday cake page. Before, 48 clicks from 2,400 impressions. That is 2 percent.

23
00:03:20.260 --> 00:03:28.780
After, 204 clicks from 5,100 impressions. That is 4 percent, and clicks are more than four times higher.

24
00:03:30.030 --> 00:03:41.140
She spots wedding cake price Ibadan with 1,300 impressions but only 9 clicks. Her wedding page title just says Wedding. She rewrites it with prices.

25
00:03:42.390 --> 00:03:46.760
She notes the date of the change, so she can check that search again in 6 weeks.

26
00:03:47.110 --> 00:03:51.760
Change one thing at a time, and give Google time to recrawl before you judge.

27
00:03:53.010 --> 00:04:04.430
Clicks are not sales, so link them to business results. Set up key events in Google Analytics 4, such as taps on your WhatsApp button, and ask new customers how they found you.

28
00:04:04.780 --> 00:04:08.890
Keep the report to one page, with one plain line under each number.

29
00:04:10.140 --> 00:04:24.350
To remember. Write for people first. Compress your photos for phones. Never buy links or stuff keywords. Work out CTR as clicks divided by impressions. And change one thing at a time, then compare.

30
00:04:25.600 --> 00:04:35.590
Now test one page for speed, check a site for spam tactics, find one search with many impressions but few clicks, and fill in your first monthly report.

31
00:04:35.940 --> 00:04:37.880
Continue with the lessons below.
